{"iteration":5,"source":"nextTransition","action":{"kind":"revise-route","story":"S2-contract-schema","role":"test-strategist","gate":"test_list","reason":"blocking smell \"reflect-testlist-defect\": reflection gate: T19 is kind:behavior (scenario_file in tests/features/S2-contract-schema.feature) but AC3-down-migration-reconstructs-code's architectural_notes explicitly require 'schema-mutating test on an isolated ephemeral migration branch.' Behavior tests connect to the shared experiment branch; running alembic downgrade -1 inside a pytest-bdd step on that branch would corrupt the post-UP schema that T13/T14/T15/T16 depend on. T19 must be kind:fitness with @pytest.mark.migration (matching T17/T18/T21's pattern), not a Gherkin scenario.; T20 is kind:behavior (scenario_file in tests/features/S2-contract-schema.feature) but AC4-round-trip-returns-to-dropped-state's architectural_notes explicitly require 'schema-mutating test (downgrade then re-upgrade) run on an isolated ephemeral migration branch.' Same corruption risk as T19: applying alembic down + re-up inside pytest-bdd step defs on the shared experiment branch would break T13-T16. T20 must be kind:fitness with @pytest.mark.migration, not a Gherkin scenario.; No S2 test-list item carries nfr_id:\"NFR-R1-migration-data-survival\", yet AC2-stock-rows-survive-drop explicitly states it 'realizes R1 at the contract boundary (R1).' T17 (invariant_id:PI4) and T18 (invariant_id:PI3) cover the intent but are untagged for R1. Since NFR-R1 declares a fitness_functions ARRAY, checkFitnessClauseCoverage enforces per-entry nfr_id coverage — but NFR-R1's array has no S2-contract-migration entry, so S2's R1 realization cannot be gated mechanically. Add nfr_id:\"NFR-R1-migration-data-survival\" to T17 (or T18) once the corresponding S2 clause is added to the array (see spec-author finding).","source":"smell:reflect-testlist-defect"},"stateBag":{"phase":"feature","buildActive":null},"at":"2026-09-17T08:53:29.245Z"}
